Compile whisper.cpp and ggml with optimisation on MSVC

With the Visual Studio generator the cmake crate replaces CMake's flags
for the build type (/O2 /Ob2 /DNDEBUG for Release) with the compiler
flags it passes on (/MD and so on), which carry no optimisation level:
the generated projects had an empty <Optimization>, so cl.exe compiled
whisper.cpp and ggml with its default, no optimisation. Their CPU side
(decoder loop, graph building, sampling) then slowed CUDA and Vulkan
alike. Measured on an RTX 5080 with large-v3-turbo on 42 s of speech
(PC check, flash attention on): CUDA 438 to 454 ms before, 292 ms after;
Vulkan 501 to 699 ms before, 281 ms after.

diff --git a/build.rs b/build.rs
index 6449916..061105f 100644
--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -269,10 +269,12 @@ fn main() {
         // so we build with optimizations even in debug mode
         config.define("CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE", "RelWithDebInfo");
         config.cxxflag("-DWHISPER_DEBUG");
+        msvc_optimize(&mut config, "-O2 -Ob1");
     } else {
         // we're in release mode, explicitly set to release mode
         // see also https://codeberg.org/tazz4843/whisper-rs/issues/226
         config.define("CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE", "Release");
+        msvc_optimize(&mut config, "-O2 -Ob2 -DNDEBUG");
     }
 
     // Allow passing any WHISPER or CMAKE compile flags
@@ -393,3 +395,14 @@ fn get_whisper_cpp_version(whisper_root: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<Op
 
     Ok(None)
 }
+
+/// With the Visual Studio generator the cmake crate replaces CMake's flags
+/// for the build type (/O2 /Ob2 /DNDEBUG for Release) with the compiler
+/// flags it passes on (/MD and so on), which have no optimisation level, so
+/// whisper.cpp and ggml were compiled without optimisation. These flags go
+/// into CMAKE_<LANG>_FLAGS and CMAKE_<LANG>_FLAGS_<BUILD_TYPE> both.
+fn msvc_optimize(config: &mut Config, flags: &str) {
+    if env::var("CARGO_CFG_TARGET_ENV").as_deref() == Ok("msvc") {
+        config.cflag(flags).cxxflag(flags);
+    }
+}
